To preview all the pages on your local machine, ensure your frontend server is running (`npm run dev` in the `frontend` folder). 

Here is the complete list of all frontend page URLs and their functions:

### 🏠 Public Pages
These are accessible to everyone immediately.
| Page Name | URL |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Landing Page** | `http://localhost:3000/` |
| **Login** | `http://localhost:3000/login` |
| **Register** | `http://localhost:3000/register` |
| **Forgot Password** | `http://localhost:3000/forgot-password` |
| **Reset Password** | `http://localhost:3000/reset-password?token=YOUR_TOKEN` |

### 📊 Dashboard & Features
*Note: These require you to be **logged in**.*
| Page Name | URL |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Main Dashboard** | `http://localhost:3000/dashboard` |
| **Document Manager** | `http://localhost:3000/documents` |
| **AI Chat Console** | `http://localhost:3000/chat` |
| **Billing & Pricing** | `http://localhost:3000/billing` |
| **Account Settings** | `http://localhost:3000/settings` |

### 🛡️ Admin Panel
*Note: This requires an **Admin Role**.*
| Page Name | URL |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Admin Dashboard** | `http://localhost:3000/admin` |

---

### 💡 Quick Commands
- **Start Backend**: `cd backend; npm run dev`
- **Start Frontend**: `cd frontend; npm run dev`
- **View DB Data**: `cd backend; npx prisma studio` (Opens on `http://localhost:5555`)

